<title>FRANCE: HORSE RACING-PRIX GANAY RESULT.</title>
<headline>HORSE RACING-PRIX GANAY RESULT.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Result of the group one Prix Ganay</p>
<p>for four-year-olds and upwards, run over one mile two and a half</p>
<p>furlongs (2.1 kms) at Longchamp on Sunday:</p>
<p>1. Helissio (ridden by Olivier Peslier)</p>
<p>2. Le Destin (Thierry Gillet)</p>
<p>3. Pilsudski (Michael Kinane)</p>
<p>8 ran.</p>
<p>Distances: 6 lengths, 1 1/2.</p>
<p>Winner owned by Enrique Sarasola and trained in France by</p>
<p>Elie Lellouche.</p>
<p>Value to the winner: 94,276 dollars</p>
<p>Pari-Mutuel (includes a one-franc stake): Win 1.60; places</p>
<p>1.10, 1.10, 1.10. Dual forecast 22.90.</p>
</text>
